# Role: Senior Creative Game & Frontend Developer
Goal: Build a high-polish, presentation-ready Battleship Web Game Show in a single standalone HTML file (`index.html`).

## Technical Stack & Constraints
- Single Standalone File: Deliver everything in `index.html` (run directly via double-click on browser without server or build tools).
- Embed Data: Read `questions.json` and embed its structure directly into a JavaScript constant `GAME_DATA` inside `index.html` to avoid local `file://` CORS restrictions.
- Zero Assets Dependency: Strictly no external image/audio files required. All graphics, ships, pegs, and audio synthesized natively.
- Styling: Tailwind CSS CDN (`<script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>`).
- Typography: Google Fonts ("Be Vietnam Pro").
- Icons: Lucide Icons CDN (`<script src="https://unpkg.com/lucide@latest"></script>`).
- Celebration: Canvas Confetti CDN (`<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/canvas-confetti@1.9.3/dist/confetti.browser.min.js"></script>`).
- Audio: Native Web Audio API synthesis for all sound FX (sonar ping, cannon blast explosion, ocean splash, chime correct, buzzer timeout, fleet alarm siren, heavy bass detonation, victory fanfare). Must handle browser Autoplay resume on first user interaction.

## UI/UX & Visual Standards (Hasbro Battleship Style)
- Theme: Dark Arcade / Tactical Naval Command (Slate-950 background, glowing cyan & amber neon borders, frosted glass cards).
- Projector Optimization: High contrast, large bold coordinates (A-J, 1-10), readable from distance.
- Tactical Grid 10x10: Glowing grid lines, crosshair targeting reticle `[ ]` on cell hover.
- 3D Tactical Pegs:
  - White Pegs ⚪ (Miss): Metallic 3D bevel circles with water ripple pulse.
# Role: Senior Creative Game & Frontend Developer
Goal: Build a high-polish, presentation-ready Battleship Web Game Show in a single standalone HTML file (`index.html`).

## Technical Stack & Constraints
- Single Standalone File: Deliver everything in `index.html` (run directly via double-click on browser without server or build tools).
- Embed Data: Read `questions.json` and embed its structure directly into a JavaScript constant `GAME_DATA` inside `index.html` to avoid local `file://` CORS restrictions.
- Zero Assets Dependency: Strictly no external image/audio files required. All graphics, ships, pegs, and audio synthesized natively.
- Styling: Tailwind CSS CDN (`<script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>`).
- Typography: Google Fonts ("Be Vietnam Pro").
- Icons: Lucide Icons CDN (`<script src="https://unpkg.com/lucide@latest"></script>`).
- Celebration: Canvas Confetti CDN (`<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/canvas-confetti@1.9.3/dist/confetti.browser.min.js"></script>`).
- Audio: Native Web Audio API synthesis for all sound FX (sonar ping, cannon blast explosion, ocean splash, chime correct, buzzer timeout, fleet alarm siren, heavy bass detonation, victory fanfare). Must handle browser Autoplay resume on first user interaction.

## UI/UX & Visual Standards (Hasbro Battleship Style)
- Theme: Dark Arcade / Tactical Naval Command (Slate-950 background, glowing cyan & amber neon borders, frosted glass cards).
- Projector Optimization: High contrast, large bold coordinates (A-J, 1-10), readable from distance.
- Tactical Grid 10x10: Glowing grid lines, crosshair targeting reticle `[ ]` on cell hover.
- 3D Tactical Pegs:
  - White Pegs ⚪ (Miss): Metallic 3D bevel circles with water ripple pulse.
  - Red Pegs 🔴 (Hit): Glowing 3D red sphere with flame halo and amber backlight.
- Top-Down Warship Art (SVG Vector):
  - Detailed top-down blueprint silhouettes (gun turrets, bridge tower, bow, stern) rendered directly across contiguous cells when ships sink.
  - Glowing colored tactical bounding box around destroyed ships.
- Dramatic "SHIP SUNK!" Cutscene:
  - 2.5s cinematic overlay with red letterbox laser bars, bold 3D "SHIP SUNK!" arcade text, fleet siren + heavy explosion sound, screen shake, and confetti celebration.
- Fleet Status & Mini Radar Map:
  - Side panel tracking health/sunk status of all 5 ships.
  - 10x10 Mini Radar Map displaying overall battle overview.
- Interactive Features:
  - 30-second question countdown with progress bar and urgent pulse at last 5 seconds.
  - Steal turn mechanism for remaining 3 teams when active team fails or times out.
  - Editable team names by clicking on team badges.
  - Live Battle Event Log ticker.
  - Sudden Death tie-breaker modal for tied leaders.